{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"yes\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"yes\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"The spacing of stimulation trains and insertion of stimulation pauses with TBS-DBS might represent a double-edged sword for DBS application.\",\n    \"On the one hand, there is evidence of re-emerging tremor during spaced thalamic deep brain stimulation depending on the length and timing of the stimulation pause.\",\n    \"The finding of impaired, short-term efficacy in tremor suppression by non-continuous DBS was interpreted as the inability to mask burst-driver inputs to the thalamus.\",\n    \"On the other hand, we assumed TBS-DBS to be potentially advantageous for gait due to the following reasons: (1) Previous studies suggested that nonregular patterns of STN-DBS with pauses were more effective in desynchronizing neural activity in PD and treatment-refractory obsessive-compulsive disorder compared to standard STN-DBS.\",\n    \"TBS-DBS with its temporal patterning might slowly, progressively increase its subthalamic efficacy in the long-term by beneficial neuroplastic effects from TBS-DBS.\",\n    \"In the visuo-tectal systems or the hippocampus it was shown that bursting effects play a predominant role in determining the precision and specificity of synaptic plasticity.\",\n    \"Since axial symptoms might change over days, the EEG might potentially point to advantageous long-term changes, which could not be proven in that acute experimental setting.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"In this monocentric, randomised, double-blind, short-term study, 12 age-matched controls (11 male, age 59 ± 8 years) and 15 PD participants (14 male, age 62 ± 9 years, disease duration 15 ± 6 years) with subthalamic stimulation (76 ± 39 months) were assessed with clinical scores (FoG-Course, MDS-UPDRS) and a standardized gait course simulating everyday life situations.\",\n    \"The primary outcome, the relative change of FoG-Course by DBS, was not superior with TBS-DBS compared to cDBS in the entire sample.\",\n    \"All 15 PD participants were asked to subjectively rate the TBS-DBS condition when still blinded. 4 PD participants rated TBS better (4 PD participants), equal (3 PD participants) or worse (8 PD participants) compared to cDBS.\",\n    \"The aims of the present, single-center, randomized, double-blind study were to (1) assess the effects of bilateral TBS-DBS on gait and FoG in PD patients by using established clinical scores, quantitative gait analysis with wearable kinematic sensors in real life gait conditions and (2) cortical network changes measured by a mobile EEG system.\",\n    \"In detail, the TBS pattern consists of 5 cycles per second, with each cycle containing 0.1s bursts at 200 Hz followed by a 0.1s pause.\",\n    \"The most important limitation in the evaluation of patterned DBS algorithms is the assessment of short-term effects of TBS-DBS on gait within one day, since the effects of patterned DBS might evolve over time and axial symptoms typically respond over a longer time course.\",\n    \"For the exploration of the full effect strength, a long-term evaluation of TBS-DBS would be necessary, which has not been performed here in the randomised study of short-term effects.\",\n    \"On the one hand, there is evidence of re-emerging tremor during spaced thalamic deep brain stimulation depending on the length and timing of the stimulation pause.\",\n    \"The finding of impaired, short-term efficacy in tremor suppression by non-continuous DBS was interpreted as the inability to mask burst-driver inputs to the thalamus.\",\n    \"TBS-DBS with its temporal patterning might slowly, progressively increase its subthalamic efficacy in the long-term by beneficial neuroplastic effects from TBS-DBS.\",\n    \"In the visuo-tectal systems or the hippocampus it was shown that bursting effects play a predominant role in determining the precision and specificity of synaptic plasticity.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"两个判断可以同时成立，并不矛盾。report_supported为yes：论文Discussion第216—232行明确提出了TBS-DBS的双重机制假说。一方面，刺激暂停可能使丘脑的burst-driver病理性输入重新显现，从而削弱短期疗效；另一方面，间歇性刺激可能通过神经活动去同步化及长期神经可塑性改善步态。论文还明确提及轴性症状可能随时间发生变化。因此，将该论文作为H19和H20竞争性机制假说的重要文献来源，有直接的全文依据。\\n\\njudge_supported为yes：但上述内容属于作者结合既往研究提出的机制解释，并非本试验直接验证的机制。具体而言：（1）研究是15名帕金森病患者参与的单中心、随机、双盲、短期研究；主要FoG-Course结局未显示TBS-DBS优于cDBS。（2）15人中只有4人主观评价TBS-DBS更好、3人评价相等，另外8人评价更差。（3）研究使用移动EEG测量的是皮层活动，并未直接记录STN神经活动。（4）TBS-DBS采用固定的0.1秒暂停，没有比较不同暂停时长。（5）研究在单日实验中评估短期效应，没有进行长期随访。\\n\\n尤其重要的是，H19的burst-driver输入重新显现，原文明确指向既往间歇性丘脑DBS的震颤研究（thalamic deep brain stimulation），随后才将其作为解释TBS-DBS步态及FOG短期疗效可能较差的假说。H20的神经可塑性论证则主要引用视觉顶盖系统、海马及突触可塑性研究，并明确承认本研究没有进行长期验证。值得补充的是，作者还引用了另一项PD患者长期TBS-DBS研究，但这同样不能替代本试验自身的长期证据。\\n\\n最终结论：报告将该研究用于构建两种竞争性机制假说，没有违背全文；指控者认为该试验不能作为这两种机制的直接实验支持，也完全符合全文。必须区分文献对机制假说的提出和本试验对机制的实证检验。不能因为机制没有在本试验中得到验证，就认定报告引用该论文构建假说属于误读。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "84ff5933-8171-42ed-801f-49ce56c0f52e", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261114T073951944139Z", "elapsed_seconds": 136.594, "completed_utc": "2026-11-14T07:42:08.554856+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "64955acbb1e162cd8b7353dff96e2af428db7e9722c2002c617f74c2657b2a64", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "Nozomi Kasaki / gpt4", "account_sha256": "bbd4fd636d4b6714d2b42b89e341bdb5bbe7c34f7d141aec76b444be8343fe54", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261114T073951944139Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "b61c7024be20a88bbb344cadff3d01ec396f8edcaf0fc2aa7f1e0f7ceb34101f"}}}
